{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>This is what pertains to the Levites.</b> By way of the plain sense (peshat): this is the fixed portion." "<b>And by way of the Midrash:</b> 'This is what pertains to the Levites' — 'this' (זאת) is nothing but Torah, as it is said (Deuteronomy 4): ״וזאת התורה״, and the Levites were the teachers of Torah, in the manner of what is written (Deuteronomy 33): ״יורו משפטיך ליעקב ותורתך לישראל״." "<b>And by way of the Kabbalah:</b> 'This is what pertains to the Levites' is like (Psalms 118:23): ״מאת ה׳ היתה זאת״, and it is the covenant, as it is said (Genesis 17:10): ״זאת בריתי״, and concerning the tribe of Levi it is written (Deuteronomy 33:9): ״ובריתך ינצורו״, and in the numbering of the Levites it is said (Numbers 3:39): ״על פי ה׳ כי זאת היא מדתם״." "<b>From twenty-five years old and upward they shall come to serve in the service of the Tent of Meeting.</b> But earlier, in the parashah of Naso (Numbers 4), it says: ״ומבן שלשים שנה״ — 'from thirty years old.'" "<b>And by way of the plain sense (peshat):</b> from thirty years old for the labor of carrying burdens, and from twenty-five years old for the service of the Tent. And this is why it says here ״לצבא צבא״ — to be counted with the host of those who serve in their watches alongside the elders." "<b>And by way of the</b> Midrash: our Rabbis, of blessed memory, [say] — 'from twenty-five years old' to teach them the laws of the service for five years, and 'from thirty' for the service. From here they inferred: any student who has not seen a favorable sign in his study for five years, will never again see it."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:30:56.316891078Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}